{
    "word": "fenny",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "61fcb187-e349-3e25-8623-2844570cbcc4",
                "word": "fenny",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "4e533818-2d87-48b4-ab3b-8a0a49412d24",
                        "entry_id": "61fcb187-e349-3e25-8623-2844570cbcc4",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more fenny"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "b6f5bf88-14cd-43df-860c-4fe8992ce6d7",
                        "entry_id": "61fcb187-e349-3e25-8623-2844570cbcc4",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most fenny"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1b46f815-51a9-3851-a68e-b77dbb1134cb",
                        "entry_id": "61fcb187-e349-3e25-8623-2844570cbcc4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Characteristic of or resembling a fen (“characteristically alkaline wetland containing peat below the waterline”); marshy, swampy; also, of land: containing a fen or fens."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6fa5db41-d69f-4ae1-8005-5530f4c29d3f",
                                "sense_id": "1b46f815-51a9-3851-a68e-b77dbb1134cb",
                                "text": "[I]nnumerable popingayes of ſundry kindes are found chattering in the groues of thoſe fenny places."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "254a611f-d10a-40a5-ad88-aa350ed1a365",
                                "sense_id": "1b46f815-51a9-3851-a68e-b77dbb1134cb",
                                "text": "[F]or ſo many faire and Nauigable Riuers ſo neere adioyning, and piercing thorovv ſo faire a naturall Land, free from any inundations, or large Fenny vnvvholſome Marſhes, I haue not ſeene, read, nor heard of: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e298c63d-da50-4109-9271-13257655d4cd",
                                "sense_id": "1b46f815-51a9-3851-a68e-b77dbb1134cb",
                                "text": "Elephant. Elephantus. […] Their differences are according to place; ſo ſome live in fenny places, ſome on mountaines, ſome in fields, others in vvoods, &c."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e43e9bc-13f3-48ab-b39a-d0762444459c",
                                "sense_id": "1b46f815-51a9-3851-a68e-b77dbb1134cb",
                                "text": "It is a custom with the northern lovers to divert themselves with a song whilst they journey through the fenny moors to pay a visit to their mistresses."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e49f5f2c-f5e0-31e8-a974-fd2677ddad10",
                        "entry_id": "61fcb187-e349-3e25-8623-2844570cbcc4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Now chiefly of plants: growing or living in a fen."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "535c0c35-9803-4754-818c-eaf1b0e5ad92",
                                "sense_id": "e49f5f2c-f5e0-31e8-a974-fd2677ddad10",
                                "text": "A fenny gooſe, even as her fleſhe is blacker, ſtoorer, unholſomer, ſo is her feather, for the ſame cauſe, courſer, ſtoorer, and rougher, and therefore I have heard very good fletchers ſay, that the ſecond fether in ſome place is better than the pinion in other ſome."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1ea899e-f96f-4dd1-b67d-e9a35b7e775e",
                                "sense_id": "e49f5f2c-f5e0-31e8-a974-fd2677ddad10",
                                "text": "Fillet of a Fenny Snake, / In the Cauldron boyle and bake: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7e645896-9f88-4585-a7d3-df876d6093ef",
                                "sense_id": "e49f5f2c-f5e0-31e8-a974-fd2677ddad10",
                                "text": "Of the Indian Dragons there are alſo ſaid to be tvvo kindes, one of them fenny, and liuing in the Marſhes, vvhich are ſlovv of pace and vvithout combes on their heades like females: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a34f6734-9508-4a5c-92ee-2e375957c80d",
                                "sense_id": "e49f5f2c-f5e0-31e8-a974-fd2677ddad10",
                                "text": "Godvvit. […] they are a fenny fovvl, and live of VVorms, about River banks: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "18f2c9d7-e18b-4428-9a0c-25cfc554b3a9",
                                "sense_id": "e49f5f2c-f5e0-31e8-a974-fd2677ddad10",
                                "text": "The hungry Crocodile, and hiſſing Snake / Lurk in the troubl'd Stream and fenny Brake: […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e210243a-efa9-426e-8de7-3e532133dccd",
                                "sense_id": "e49f5f2c-f5e0-31e8-a974-fd2677ddad10",
                                "text": "Paths there were many, / Winding through palmy fern, and rushes fenny, / And ivy banks; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3dd851a4-a28c-3faf-9765-0e861de4ff4d",
                        "entry_id": "61fcb187-e349-3e25-8623-2844570cbcc4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Muddy; hence, dirty, filthy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "also",
                            "figuratively",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "86a70c74-6af2-4e02-8e46-61c04b63e45c",
                                "sense_id": "3dd851a4-a28c-3faf-9765-0e861de4ff4d",
                                "text": "Lord vvhat a nothing is this little Span, / VVe call a Man! / VVhat fenny traſh maintaines the ſmooth'ring fires / Of his desires!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c4ebb914-3c7c-468f-845e-493a2921fa63",
                        "source_entry_id": "61fcb187-e349-3e25-8623-2844570cbcc4",
                        "source_sense_description": "characteristic of or resembling a fen; of land: containing a fen or fens — see also marshy, swampy",
                        "target_lang_word": "moorig",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "moorig",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b68ba0f8-35d3-33cb-8ffa-2b23becc7ae9",
                                        "entry_id": "bf2b42f5-e496-3423-a65d-41b70326d680",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "einen aus Moor bestehenden Boden aufweisend; in der Art eines Moores"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f9e951a-bfc0-4165-9c5a-cd7283533bb4",
                                                "sense_id": "b68ba0f8-35d3-33cb-8ffa-2b23becc7ae9",
                                                "text": "„Heidelbeeren bevorzugen Moorbeeterde, also einen moorigen und sandigen Grund.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eed8e5f8-c2d0-40e7-be7c-9b67e93afeb3",
                                                "sense_id": "b68ba0f8-35d3-33cb-8ffa-2b23becc7ae9",
                                                "text": "„Auch Glockenheide (Erica tetralix) ist auf sauren, moorigen Boden angewiesen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e66f4c84-8da0-4764-98c5-799010bb0efa",
                                                "sense_id": "b68ba0f8-35d3-33cb-8ffa-2b23becc7ae9",
                                                "text": "„Ein schmaler, rund 500 Meter langer Pfad führt über moorigen Grund, Wasserläufe, Gestrüpp und umgestürzte Bäume.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b5786b4-40a2-4f3b-8026-52b9d35f205b",
                                                "sense_id": "b68ba0f8-35d3-33cb-8ffa-2b23becc7ae9",
                                                "text": "„Bis dahin war die schleswig-holsteinische Westküste ein Labyrinth an Inseln, Prielen und moorigen Marschen gewesen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3937e49e-b9ec-4ff9-9593-e1350d7f92df",
                                                "sense_id": "b68ba0f8-35d3-33cb-8ffa-2b23becc7ae9",
                                                "text": "„Der Boden sei teils moorig, teils sandig und mitunter wenig standfest.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7762adc5-3f1c-4eae-b84c-065d555ae7ee",
                                                "sense_id": "b68ba0f8-35d3-33cb-8ffa-2b23becc7ae9",
                                                "text": "„Ganz früher war die Reise ins südlich gelegene Garreler Feld sehr beschwerlich, weil die Gegend sehr sumpfig und moorig war.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8091ca73-047a-406e-9a04-546f90b64e1f",
                                                "sense_id": "b68ba0f8-35d3-33cb-8ffa-2b23becc7ae9",
                                                "text": "„Ein unwirklicher, urwüchsiger, auch gespenstischer Wald ist der Darßwald, moosig, moorig, aus knorrigen Buchen und bizarr geformten Kiefern, zu den Seiten Blaubeerbüsche, Wacholdersträucher und riesengroße Ameisenhaufen, die wie dicke fette Gnome am Wegesrand hocken.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cba15107-7d5c-4881-8bcb-afe0863df597",
                                                "sense_id": "b68ba0f8-35d3-33cb-8ffa-2b23becc7ae9",
                                                "text": "„Vier Seen könnte man auf 14 Kilometern umrunden, wir schaffen gerade mal einen und nehmen die Serpentinenstraße zum Pic de l’Aigle, um das Plateau mit seinen teils moorigen Wasserlandschaften wenigstens von oben in seiner Fülle erfassen zu können.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
